## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/grunge_galvanizedsteel.html
- Summary (EN): Grunge Galvanized Steel generates a layered-noise pattern that imitates the crystalline surface of galvanized steel. It can be used as a mask or as a building block for detailed textures, such as steel surfaces on nails or roofs.
- Résumé (FR) : Grunge Galvanized Steel imite la surface cristalline de l'acier galvanisé par un bruit en couches, utilisable en masque ou comme brique de texture métallique.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: reference layer that sets the output size and metadata"]

- Key parameters: ["Range: Amplitude scales values before Center; Center offsets them; Mask Contrast adjusts contrast", "Pattern: Element Size (Element Scale with Per-Component Controls), Offset, Tile Size", "Distort Size, Distort Angle, Distort Scale: bend the spangle shapes in the base layer", "Secondary Distort Size and Secondary Distort Roughness: edge softness and wave roughness", "Seed: randomizes the result while keeping the same look", "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"]

- Caveats: ["Output can fall below 0 or above 1; use the Clamp options", "Complement assumes values between 0 and 1", "Fold has no visible effect when all values are positive", "Post-processing Contrast is separate from Noise Contrast", "Tile Size should match the aspect ratio of non-square images"]

